---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = '2026-09-16';
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="How VisaLang uses advertising consent, session storage, optional local storage, and legacy URL cleanup." noindex={true} enableAds={false}>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <article class="guide-article narrow-page">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="guide-summary">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <h2>What are cookies</h2>
        <p>Cookies are small text files stored in your browser. VisaLang does not currently set first-party cookies through its site code.</p>

        <h2>Local storage we use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Advertising source boundary:</strong> the current Astro source can emit the Google AdSense loader only for ad-eligible English guide pages. Tool pages and the searchable Guide Library index do not load it. This repository does not verify a deployed AdSense account, served ads, Google Privacy &amp; messaging/CMP message, regional consent path, or partner identifier behavior. Google Analytics, Cloudflare Web Analytics, and custom measurement events are not loaded or sent by the current Astro source.</li>
          <li><strong>Shared tool plan:</strong> current tools store only schema-approved plan fields in browser <code>sessionStorage</code> by default so fields can move between tools in the same tab. New results are not written to URL query parameters. Reminder dates, optional source URLs, free text and identity-like data are excluded from the shared plan.</li>
          <li><strong>Optional 30-day device copy:</strong> browser <code>localStorage</code> is used for shared tool fields only after you activate “Save on this device for 30 days.” A saved snapshot is no longer restored after expiry and is removed on a later visit; the site does not run a background timer after you close it.</li>
          <li><strong>Legacy per-tool local storage:</strong> current tool pages attempt to remove the fixed <code>visalang-tool:...</code> local-storage copies used by older tool versions on the same site origin. “Clear shared plan” repeats that cleanup. One domain cannot read or delete another domain’s storage, and browser site-data settings are the complete removal path for an old origin or when storage access is blocked.</li>
          <li><strong>Route progress:</strong> route pages can store the current route step in browser local storage. This storage also has no site-defined automatic expiry.</li>
          <li><strong>Guide filters:</strong> Guide Library filters also use page URL values so the filtered view can be restored or shared.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Measurement contract</h2>
        <p>The five tool pages expose the local-only contract version <code>t27.v1</code> for auditability. It defines aggregate-safe event names and finite enums but has no collector, cookie, beacon, fetch, XMLHttpRequest, queue, or measurement storage. Tool results and explicit checklist/ICS takeaways remain local browser behavior; a rendered unsupported or official-verification-required state is not a successful completion.</p>

        <h2>Third-party social tracking</h2>
        <p>We do not use third-party social-media tracking cookies. Third-party sites you visit from VisaLang, including official sources and advertising destinations, apply their own policies.</p>

        <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
        <p>Use the Google consent/privacy control where available to consent, use the configured non-consent path, manage options, or change a previous advertising choice. You can also manage personalised advertising through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>
        <p>“Restart this tool” resets the current form and the plan fields owned by that tool. The shared route remains when Checklist or Reminder is restarted; shared date or exam choices can be cleared by their owning tool. Use “Clear shared plan” to request removal of the tab-session state, optional device copy, and known same-origin legacy per-tool local storage. This does not remove the separately stored route-progress key. You can clear or block site storage in browser settings to remove both systems.</p>

        <h2>Legacy URL query cleanup</h2>
        <p>If an older tool link contains query values, the current tool validates compatible fixed values, discards unsupported data and removes the URL query from the address bar. Address-bar cleanup does not erase browser history or a request already recorded in historical server, proxy, CDN, analytics, or security logs. VisaLang does not claim that client-side cleanup can delete those logs.</p>

        <h2>Third-party embeds</h2>
        <p>VisaLang does not currently load third-party video or resource embeds. Following a link to an external site takes you to that site, where its own privacy and cookie policies apply.</p>

        <h2>Questions or changes</h2>
        <p>For privacy questions, use our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We update this page when our cookie, consent, analytics, or advertising approach changes.</p>

        <p class="compliance-line">See also our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
